# Accepted risks for the Trivy scan (.github/workflows/security-audit.yml). Each entry says why
# and expires, so Trivy reports it again for review on that date.

# CVE-2023-54404: zod <4.6.6, validating an unbounded array, set or map can exhaust memory.
# Reown AppKit brings it in: @reown/appkit-wallet pins zod 3.22.4 and the Coinbase CDP SDK (via
# @base-org/account) needs ^3.25.76. No zod 3 release has the change, and per the advisory no
# release fixes unbounded schemas at all, so forcing zod 4 would risk the wallet without closing
# the issue. zod runs only in the browser, in the wallet chunk loaded when a user connects, so the
# worst case is the user's own tab running out of memory. Revisit when AppKit or the CDP SDK
# moves to a newer zod.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2027-01-31
